  "scope": "Known spin-matrix product-sphere spectra yield a controlled geometric heat-kernel window and its first two radius variations, including the Einstein curvature coefficient. The complete fixed-size scalar determinant has the opposite sign of fixed-volume shape curvature, with a proved fourth-power angular-cutoff lower bound; the omitted ultraviolet contribution cannot be dropped. The matrix geometry and regulator window are supplied. Microscopic locality, Lorentzian gravity, state selection, gravitational constraints, and a TOE remain unproved."
